{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"be549cf605f93aa3164b0550875d0abd189c78f307e1264cbe21970dbdb6cf4e","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI complexity-baseline gate","key_entities":["scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py","lock_against_base","_fetch_base_ceilings_from_main",".github/complexity-baseline.json","src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py"],"problem_keywords":["complexity gate","baseline comparison","merge base","ceiling reduction","un-rebased branches"],"propositions":["The complexity lock compares branch baseline against main tip rather than merge base, causing false violations when main lowers a ceiling and un-rebased branches carry the old baseline.","Every future ceiling reduction on main breaks all un-rebased branches identically by appearing as a raised ceiling from the branch's perspective, punishing the shrinking the ratchet exists to reward.","The fix compares branch baseline against merge-base(main, HEAD) and reads the baseline at that commit, so only changes the branch itself made can violate lock rules.","The fetch depth must increase from --depth=1 to allow merge-base computation, with fallback to main-tip comparison and explicit notification if no merge base can be computed."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787477642035158001,"uuid":"e66462c5-d8fe-4a13-94ea-19f45e05301a"}